# Files copied into every worktree Claude Code creates with git.
#
# A worktree is a fresh checkout, so gitignored local config is absent and the
# first build in a new worktree fails for reasons unrelated to the ticket.
# Syntax is .gitignore syntax. Only files that match AND are gitignored are
# copied, so tracked files (.env.example) are never duplicated.
#
# Not processed if a WorktreeCreate hook replaces the default git logic.
# Reference: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/worktrees

.env
.env.*
*.local.md
*.local.mdx

# Working documentation, so a session in a worktree can reach the decision
# records rather than re-deriving or contradicting a settled one.
#
# THE RULE SHAPE IS LOAD-BEARING, and this is measured rather than reasoned.
# The copier enumerates gitignored entries the way `git status --ignored` does,
# which COLLAPSES a wholly-ignored directory to its own name. So:
#
#   *.local.md      does NOT reach internal-docs/agents/x.local.md — the file
#                   was never an entry to match, only the directory was
#   /internal-docs/ DOES copy the whole tree — it matches that collapsed entry
#
# Verified in a fresh worktree: internal-docs/ and internal-docs/adr/ arrive
# with both ADRs. A file glob cannot reach inside; a directory pattern can.
# Do not "simplify" this to a glob.
/internal-docs/
